Neeche wala prompt **Google AI Studio ke Build prompt box mein poora paste** karna. English mein diya hai kyunki coding agent ko technical requirements clearly samajh aayengi.

# BUILD ETHAUM CARECONNECT — COMPLETE FULL-STACK APPLICATION

Act as a senior product designer, full-stack engineer, AI engineer, database architect and QA engineer.

Build a complete, polished, responsive, production-minded medical tourism web application named **EthAum CareConnect** from scratch.

This is a fresh project. Do not create just a landing page, static prototype or UI mockup. Build a functioning full-stack application with real navigation, forms, authentication, persistent database operations, backend APIs, AI features and role-based dashboards.

## 1. PRODUCT VISION

EthAum CareConnect connects international patients with hospitals, doctors and medical tourism service providers. It helps patients discover providers, organize medical records, request treatment quotations, compare options and coordinate their healthcare journey.

The platform is a coordination and discovery service. It must never claim to diagnose a disease, prescribe treatment or determine clinical suitability.

## 2. TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

Use:

- React + TypeScript for the frontend.
- Modern component-based architecture.
- Node.js server-side runtime for backend APIs.
- Firebase Authentication for user identity and Google sign-in.
- Cloud Firestore for persistent application data.
- Firebase Storage or another secure server-controlled file storage solution for documents.
- Gemini API through server-side code only.
- Three.js, React Three Fiber and Drei for the interactive 3D globe.
- Framer Motion for interface animations.
- Lucide icons.
- Reusable components, clean types and maintainable folder structure.

Use the platform's native Firebase setup flow. If Firebase enablement is offered, ask me to approve it and complete the integration after approval.

Never expose Gemini API keys, service credentials or privileged Firebase credentials in browser code. Never hardcode secrets.

## 3. DESIGN SYSTEM

Create a distinctive premium futuristic HealthTech experience.

Visual identity:

- Background: midnight navy (#070B18).
- Secondary surfaces: #0D1428 and #111B32.
- Primary accent: electric cyan (#35D5F5).
- Secondary accent: vivid blue and restrained violet.
- Text: high-contrast white and muted blue-grey.
- Typography: Space Grotesk for headings and Inter for body text.
- Rounded cards, subtle borders, controlled glassmorphism and elegant shadows.
- Strong visual hierarchy and generous spacing.
- Smooth micro-interactions and meaningful transitions.
- Avoid excessive gradients, clutter and generic hospital templates.

The website should feel like a premium international HealthTech startup.

## 4. PUBLIC LANDING PAGE

Build a cinematic homepage with:

A. Navigation

- EthAum CareConnect logo and brand identity.
- Treatments, Destinations, Hospitals, How It Works, About.
- Sign in and Get Started actions.
- Responsive mobile navigation.

B. Hero section

- Large headline: "Your Healthcare Journey, Connected."
- Supporting text explaining international treatment discovery and coordination.
- Primary CTA: Explore Hospitals.
- Secondary CTA: Start Your Medical Journey.
- Interactive 3D Earth/globe using Three.js and React Three Fiber.
- Glowing destination markers, animated connection arcs, subtle particles and floating healthcare data elements.
- Allow users to interact with the globe and explore destination markers.
- Include a graceful static fallback if WebGL is unavailable.
- Optimize 3D performance for laptops and mobile devices.

C. Landing page sections

- Featured treatment categories.
- International destinations.
- Featured hospitals and doctors.
- How the platform works.
- AI-powered coordination features.
- Patient journey timeline.
- Trust, privacy and transparency section.
- FAQ.
- Strong footer with navigation and contact details.

Do not invent hospital partnerships, certifications, success rates, ratings or medical credentials. Clearly label all sample content as demo data.

## 5. AUTHENTICATION AND ROLES

Create working authentication:

- Email/password registration and login.
- Google sign-in where Firebase supports it.
- Logout.
- Protected routes.
- Persistent sessions.
- Form validation and useful error messages.

Support these roles:

1. Patient.
2. Provider.
3. Admin.

New users should complete role-specific onboarding. Never allow a user to grant themselves admin privileges through an ordinary signup form.

## 6. PATIENT DASHBOARD

Create a premium dashboard with sidebar navigation and responsive layout.

Pages:

- Overview.
- My Medical Cases.
- Find Hospitals.
- Find Doctors.
- AI Medical Case Assistant.
- Compare Quotations.
- Medical Documents.
- Appointments.
- Messages.
- Patient Journey.
- Notifications.
- Profile and Settings.

Dashboard overview should show:

- Active cases.
- Pending quotations.
- Upcoming appointments.
- Journey progress.
- Recent activity.
- Recommended next actions.

All dashboard figures must come from database records or clearly labelled demo records.

## 7. MEDICAL CASE MANAGEMENT

Allow a patient to:

- Create a medical case.
- Enter treatment category, country preference, preferred language, budget range and travel preferences.
- Add a short description of their medical needs.
- Upload relevant medical documents.
- Edit and view their cases.
- Track case status.

Use clear statuses:\
Draft, Submitted, Under Review, Matching, Quotations Received, Consultation, Booked, In Treatment, Aftercare, Closed.

Validate all forms and persist changes to Firestore.

## 8. AI CASE ASSISTANT

Implement a real Gemini-powered assistant through a secure server endpoint.

Features:

- Summarize user-provided medical case descriptions.
- Organize information into a structured case summary.
- Extract non-diagnostic administrative details from uploaded records when technically supported.
- Generate questions the patient may ask a qualified doctor.
- Explain the platform's process and help with coordination.
- Help patients understand quotation fields.

Strict safety rules:

- No diagnosis.
- No prescription.
- No treatment recommendations presented as medical advice.
- No prediction of patient outcomes.
- No claims that AI can determine clinical suitability.
- Clearly label AI-generated summaries.
- Include a prominent notice that a qualified clinician must review medical information.
- If a request is medically urgent, advise contacting an appropriate medical professional or emergency service.

Do not send private records to Gemini without an explicit user action and consent. Minimize transmitted data.

## 9. HOSPITAL AND DOCTOR DISCOVERY

Create searchable provider listings with:

- Search by name, destination and specialty.
- Filters for treatment category, country and budget range.
- Provider profile pages.
- Hospital description.
- Available specialties.
- Location.
- Languages.
- Services and contact/request information.

Use fictional demo providers and clearly mark them as examples. Never fabricate real-world accreditation or verification.

## 10. EXPLAINABLE PROVIDER MATCHING

Build a transparent preference-based matching system.

Compare patient preferences with provider listing data:

- Destination preference.
- Treatment category.
- Budget range.
- Language preference.
- Other non-clinical preferences.

Show a clear breakdown of why a provider appears in the results.

Never label the score as medical suitability, clinical success probability or a guaranteed recommendation. Clearly state that the score reflects preference matching only and does not replace clinician evaluation.

## 11. QUOTATION COMPARISON

Patients should be able to receive and compare provider quotations.

Include:

- Total estimated cost.
- Currency.
- Included services.
- Excluded services.
- Estimated duration.
- Accommodation and transport details, if supplied.
- Validity date.
- Payment and cancellation terms.
- Provider notes.

Allow patients to compare quotations side by side and request clarification.

Clearly distinguish estimates from confirmed costs. Never invent a quote or imply a payment has occurred.

## 12. PROVIDER DASHBOARD

Create a separate protected provider experience:

- Overview.
- Incoming patient leads.
- Medical cases shared with the provider.
- Case status updates.
- Quotation creation and editing.
- Appointment requests.
- Messages.
- Provider profile management.
- Analytics.
- Settings.

Provider users must only access cases and documents that have been explicitly shared with them and for which they have authorization.

## 13. ADMIN DASHBOARD

Create an admin interface for authorized admin accounts:

- User management.
- Provider management.
- Case oversight.
- Content management.
- Reports and platform activity.
- Audit logs.

Admin privileges must be assigned securely, not by trusting a client-side role value.

## 14. PATIENT JOURNEY TRACKER

Build a visual timeline:

Discover → Create Case → Upload Records → Case Review → Provider Matching → Quote Comparison → Shortlist → Consultation Request → Provider Selection → Booking → Treatment → Aftercare → Review.

Show timestamps and status updates when available. Make the current stage visually clear.

## 15. MESSAGING AND NOTIFICATIONS

Implement persistent in-app conversations and notifications.

Users should be able to:

- View conversations.
- Send and receive messages.
- See timestamps.
- Mark notifications as read.
- Receive updates when case or quotation status changes.

Enforce authorization so users cannot access conversations they do not belong to.

## 16. DATA MODEL

Design Firestore collections and document relationships for:

- users
- providers
- medicalCases
- documents
- quotations
- appointments
- conversations
- messages
- notifications
- journeyEvents
- auditLogs

Add createdAt, updatedAt, ownership and relevant status fields. Use server-side validation for sensitive operations.

Create Firestore security rules that enforce role-based and ownership-based access. Never rely only on frontend route protection.

## 17. FILE SECURITY

Implement secure document upload:

- Validate file type and file size.
- Restrict access to authorized users.
- Store metadata and ownership.
- Do not expose public medical document URLs.
- Do not log medical document contents.
- Include consent and document deletion flows.
- Do not use real patient records in demo data.

## 18. FUNCTIONALITY REQUIREMENTS

Every visible action must work:

- Navigation.
- Login and registration.
- Search and filters.
- Forms.
- Uploads.
- Dashboard cards.
- Case creation and editing.
- Quotation comparison.
- Messages.
- Notifications.
- Profile settings.
- Logout.

No dead buttons, empty placeholder routes, fake integrations or buttons that only show success messages without completing the operation.

If an external service is not configured, show an honest setup or demo-state message.

## 19. DEMO EXPERIENCE

Create realistic but entirely fictional demo records for:

- Hospitals.
- Doctors.
- Patient cases.
- Quotations.
- Appointments.
- Journey progress.

Clearly mark all seeded content as demo data. Do not present fictional patient stories as real testimonials.

## 20. RESPONSIVE DESIGN AND ACCESSIBILITY

Support desktop, tablet and mobile.\
Use accessible labels, keyboard navigation, appropriate contrast and reduced-motion preferences.\
Ensure the 3D globe does not block page navigation or make mobile performance unusable.

## 21. ENGINEERING QUALITY

- Use TypeScript types throughout.
- Keep frontend and server-side code separated.
- Use reusable components.
- Handle loading, empty, success and error states.
- Validate inputs on both client and server.
- Avoid duplicate components and unnecessary dependencies.
- Avoid giant single-file implementations.
- Add meaningful error handling.
- Never put privileged operations in client-side code.

## 22. README AND HANDOVER

Create a README with:

- Project overview.
- Features.
- Technology stack.
- Architecture.
- Firebase setup.
- Gemini API setup.
- Environment variables and secrets.
- Local development instructions.
- Demo mode instructions.
- Deployment instructions.
- Security and medical AI limitations.

## 23. BUILD AND TEST PROCESS

Work in stages:

1. Generate the complete project structure and design system.
2. Build the public landing page and 3D globe.
3. Build authentication and Firebase integration.
4. Build patient dashboard and case management.
5. Build provider and admin dashboards.
6. Build Gemini assistant securely.
7. Build provider matching, quotations and journey tracker.
8. Build messaging, notifications and document security.
9. Test all routes, forms, permissions and database operations.
10. Fix build errors, runtime errors and responsive layout issues.

Do not stop after creating the homepage.

After each stage, run the available checks, inspect the live preview, fix errors and continue. Do not claim a feature is complete unless it actually works.

Start by creating the project architecture, visual design system, public landing page and interactive 3D globe. Then continue through the remaining stages until the complete application is implemented.

